# Metaphor: ReFantazio (PPSA20800) -- boot to the title screen. Verified 2026-09-23 with
# tools/screenshot at 3840x2160, Linux / Radeon 8060S (RADV), on the branch that added this file
# (#3784 sign-in dialog, #3791 glyph advance).
#
# The route depends on the title's SYSTEM save (<save root>/PPSA20800/SYSTEM), which the first-boot
# setup writes.
#
# From a CLEAN save (no PPSA20800 save directory):
#   ~20 s  language select            -> Cross (English is already highlighted)
#   ~25 s  "Proceed with English?"    -> Cross (Yes is the default)
#   ~45 s  "A network connection will enable some in-game features. Connect?"
#                                     -> Down, Cross = No. Answering Yes opens the PSN sign-in
#                                        dialog, which prosper dismisses (a signed-out console,
#                                        #3784), then "Cannot connect to network. Retry?", whose
#                                        default is Yes -- a Cross-only route loops there forever.
#   ~60 s  brightness page, then "Confirm this brightness?" (Yes default) -> Cross, Cross
#   ~90 s  warning, fiction and photosensitivity notices, ATLUS / Studio Zero / middleware logos
#   ~150 s the opening movie. It could not be skipped on a first boot in any run tried.
#   ~340 s TITLE SCREEN ("PRESS ANY BUTTON", then NEW GAME / LOAD GAME / SYSTEM), held until the
#          attract loop restarts the logos ~60 s later.
#
# With the SYSTEM save present, the same presses skip the setup and the movie: the title screen is
# up by ~40 s, and the later Cross presses select NEW GAME, which plays the storybook prologue and
# stops at name entry ("Who are you, who shall guide the protagonist?").
#
# Wall-clock timings on one machine. The presses are spaced so an early or late boot of a few
# seconds lands on the same screens; a much slower boot can shift the Down onto the language list.
20-21:cross
26-27:cross
32-33:cross
38-39:cross
44-45:cross
50-50.15:down
52-53:cross
58-59:cross
64-65:cross
70-71:cross
76-77:cross
82-83:cross
88-89:cross
94-95:cross
100-101:cross
